Choose one constrained repair for a synthetic settings dialog. A mouse can open/close the dialog, but opening fails to move keyboard focus inside; Tab can escape into the background; Escape cannot dismiss. The dialog must have a programmatic name and modality; preserve pointer behavior. Return ONLY JSON with keys schema (repair-bench.dialog-proposal.v1) and repair (one of noop, aria_only, managed_dialog), no code or markdown. Source:
<!doctype html>
<!-- Repair Bench original synthetic dialog defect: immutable evaluation fixture. -->
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Repair Bench — Dialog Focus Fixture</title><style>
body{font:17px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:42rem;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;color:#182233}
button,a{font:inherit}button{padding:.6rem 1rem;cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible{outline:4px solid #005fcc;outline-offset:3px}
#dialog-box{position:fixed;top:12%;left:12%;right:12%;margin:auto;max-width:28rem;padding:1.5rem;border:3px solid #153a5e;border-radius:12px;background:white;box-shadow:0 0 0 100vmax rgba(2,14,35,.45)}
#dialog-box h2{margin-top:0}[hidden]{display:none!important}
#outside{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}
</style></head><body>
<h1>Repair Bench: dialog focus trap</h1><p>A modal must manage keyboard focus and close with Escape—not merely declare ARIA semantics.</p>
<div id="outside"><button id="open-dialog" type="button">Open settings</button><a id="outside-link" href="#outside">Background navigation</a></div>
<div id="dialog-box" data-repair-target="dialog" hidden><h2 id="dialog-title">Settings</h2><p>Choose an option or close this modal.</p><button id="close-dialog" type="button">Close settings</button><a id="inside-link" href="#dialog-title">Dialog help</a></div>
<script>
(() => {
  const opener=document.getElementById('open-dialog');
  const box=document.getElementById('dialog-box');
  const closer=document.getElementById('close-dialog');
  function open(){box.hidden=false;}
  function close(){box.hidden=true;opener.focus();}
  opener.addEventListener('click',open);
  closer.addEventListener('click',close);
  /* TRUSTED_REPAIR_HOOK */
})();
</script></body></html>
